<title>GERMANY: Adidas shares rise on higher Q3 profit.</title>
<headline>Adidas shares rise on higher Q3 profit.</headline>
<dateline>HERZOGENAURACH, Germany 1996-11-12</dateline>
<text>
<p>Adidas AG, the German sportswear maker, said on Tuesday that net profit rose 16.7 percent to 140 million marks ($93.8 million) in the third quarter of 1996 and was up 30 percent at 324 million for the first nine months.</p>
<p>Adidas said sales jumped 34.6 percent to 1.47 billion marks in the third quarter and rose 30.7 percent to 3.71 billion marks in the first nine months.</p>
<p>Shares in Adidas rose after the announcement, climbing 2.90 marks to 136.40 marks in pre-bourse IBIS electronic trade.</p>
<p>--Frankfurt Newsroom, +49 69 756525 ($ = 1.493 German Marks)</p>
